 Endpoint

  - POST /v1/send
  - Base URL: http://192.168.1.244:3002 (your API port)

  Auth

  - Header: Authorization: Bearer <sk_...>

  Template variables

  - In templates: {{message}}, {{firstName}}, {{data.someField}}
  - data values are saved on the contact by default
  - To use a value only for this email: { "value": "...", "persistent": false }

  Example (use a template + variables)

  curl -X POST "http://192.168.1.244:3002/v1/send" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer sk_..." \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "to": "albugsp@gmail.com",
      "template": "a4772df5-1602-4f9a-93d4-1cc36a496e49",
      "data": {
        "firstName": "Al",
        "message": { "value": "<p>Hello from Plunk</p>", "persistent": false }
      }
    }'

  Example (raw subject/body instead of template)

  curl -X POST "http://192.168.1.244:3002/v1/send" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer sk_..." \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "to": "albugsp@gmail.com",
      "subject": "Hello {{firstName}}",
      "body": "<p>{{message}}</p>",
      "from": "support@gothru.co",
      "name": "GoThru",
      "data": {
        "firstName": "Al",
        "message": { "value": "Direct body example", "persistent": false }
      }
    }'

  Notes

  - If you use a template, subject/body are optional and will override template values if provided.
  - from must be a valid email from a verified domain.